    "lawCode": "Amd §84.05, Ment Hyg L",
    "lawSection": "Mental Hygiene Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7882\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to the\nimplementation of the New York achieving a better life experience (NY\nABLE) savings account act\n\n PURPOSE OF THE BILL :\n\nThis bill would facilitate access to ABLE accounts for individuals\nwith developmental disabilities and their families.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill would authorize the comptroller to enter into a contract\nwith the existing third party administrator of the NYS College Choice\nTuition Savings Program for the purpose of administering the NY\nAchieving a Better Life Experience (ABLE) savings account program and\nproviding account depositories and managers. The term of such contract\nwould expire on the same date as the contract for the administration\nof the NYS College Choice Tuition Savings Program.  Upon the\nexpiration of such contract, the comptroller may solicit proposals for\nthe purpose of administering the NY ABLE savings account program and\nthe NYS College Choice Tuition Savings Program.  Additionally, the\ncomptroller may choose to allow the programs to be administered\njointly or separately.\n\n STATEMENT IN SUPPORT :\n\nOn December 19th, 2014, President Barack Obama signed into law the\nAchieving a Better Life Experience (ABLE) Act, authorizing states to\nestablish ABLE savings accounts for qualified individuals with\ndisabilities.\n\nChapter 576 of the laws of 2015 authorized New York State to establish\na NY ABLE Savings Account Program that would allow qualified\nindividuals with developmental disabilities to save funds for\nnon-Medicaid reimbursable expenses during their adult lives. The funds\nwould accrue interest tax-free and would not be a factor in Medicaid\neligibility. This law also allows the comptroller to contract with a\n3rd party vendor in order to administer the ABLE program.\n\nAs New York continues to place greater emphasis on community-based\nservices for individuals with disabilities, the State must utilize all\navailable tools to promote independence, and provide access to such\ntools in an efficient and timely manner. This bill would accelerate\nthe implementation of the New York State ABLE savings account program\nby authorizing the Comptroller to enter into a contract with the\nexisting third party administrator of the NYS College Choice Tuition\nSavings Program for the purpose of administering the NY ABLE Savings\nAccount Program and provide the Comptroller with the option to permit\nthe programs to be administered jointly or separately by a 3rd party\nvendor.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n BUDGET IMPLICATIONS :\n\nUndetermined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediate.\n",
